ow often we we do that in  a day and how many notifications you  received so how much how which apps are  distracting you the most so on the left  here you'll see how your day breaks down  on what you spend your time on and if  you tap for further information you can  see trends over time and aspect this is  especially useful if you're trying to  change your habits you can actually see  well if you don't am I actually changing  my habits by looking at these trends and  for the apps that you want to be mindful  of we've introduced app timers and so  once you've once you've used the amount  of time you've allotted for that app the  Apple gray outs and will be paused for  the rest of the day and so anyway  getting notifications from that app  either so we've all experienced how  distracting these devices can be sitting  down in a meeting getting a notification  you know often that happens so several  people in the meeting and of course the  the devices in this case interacting  with us when when we actually don't once  it see we don't want to be distracted  we're animating and so we've introduced  gestures one of them is flipped to shush  so if you flip your phone over it won't  when distract you it won't make any  notification sounds or ring if there's  if there are incoming calls so that this  is on the latest pixel devices and  another a number of other devices from  various OMS the other feature we've  introduced is wind down so lack of sleep  caused a four hundred billion dollar  productivity head so your companies in  the US in 2016 according to a study and  for many people in this room that's  of millions of dollars so and we sort of  realized that you know getting pinged at  11 p.m. probably isn't helping with that  and because sleep is really important  and can keep us from getting enough  we've introduced this wine down feature  so wind down sets of schedule to remind  you of when to switch off at night so  you said a bedtime for your phone and it  fades to g